WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:08.440
Film Courage: This question comes in from
Flower Power.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.610
My question: How do you get producers to read
your script.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.690
I don’t have any money or connections.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.080
How do I approach this?

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.080
Just try to get lucky?

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.110
Justin Warren, Writer/Director: That’s a
really good question, I’m still trying to

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.310
figure that out.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:28.540
But the one thing that I’ve learned is that
Hollywood is incredibly relational in the

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:36.510
sense of …in theory it’s really bad because
I used to always think Why does this writer

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.409
make it and this one doesn’t?

00:00:39.409 --> 00:00:43.110
Why does this director not and why does this
one not?

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:47.569
The reality is it’s not fair.

00:00:47.569 --> 00:00:49.539
Life is not fair.

00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:53.050
Hollywood in particular is definitely not
fair.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:01:01.319
And I don’t mean that to knock it but I
think when I began to realize that there are

00:01:01.319 --> 00:01:06.100
no rules then it sort of opened up for me.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:13.951
For instance 
I know this producer friend who literally

00:01:13.951 --> 00:01:23.380
got a movie made because he knew the stunt
man who worked on the movie with that actor

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:28.170
and he asked for him to pass the script over.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:33.130
And some how it seems like in theory that
should not work, but some how that worked

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:36.740
and he attached at actor to his script and
BOOM!

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:37.740
It got made.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.369
It was a horror film or something like that.

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:47.260
But basically there’s no way.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:56.759
It seems like in my limited experience (I’ve
only been out here like 7 years) but three

00:01:56.759 --> 00:02:04.030
of that I was in film school and about four-ish
years have been trying to crack this things

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:05.929
called “Hollywood.”

00:02:05.929 --> 00:02:15.410
I’m very introverted and it’s very difficult
for me to meet people but I’ve noticed that

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:20.550
when I start becoming more relational with
people, things start to happen.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:24.790
I’m not saying that means that I’m going
to be writing on HBO next week.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:32.670
But I’ve noticed that every single year
that I’ve been out here I notice more things

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:36.550
that make LA feel smaller if that makes sense.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:41.670
For instance, the other day I was watching
a commercial and I saw a friend that I knew

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.670
on a commercial.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:43.670
And I’m like “Oh?

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:44.670
I know him.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:45.800
I met him last year.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.040
That’s him on TV.”

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.870
And then the other day I was driving down
the street and I saw a billboard and I was

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.310
“That’s Billy!

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.490
What’s Billy doing?”

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:56.940
It’s crazy.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:02.420
And every year that seems to happen a little
bit more.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:10.450
And I know that just sustained effort over
time should eventually equal “breaking into

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:13.440
Hollywood” whatever that is.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:21.060
And so I think that I definitely don’t have
an answer to that but just from my experience

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:32.180
I’ve noticed that things are starting to
happen for me by interfacing and hanging out

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:38.670
with people who are like-minded who you jive
with, who you feel a connection with because

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:45.340
I think a lot of times the piece of advice
a lot of people give is “You’ve got to

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.520
network, just network.”

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:54.300
But networking inherently feels not relational,
it feels transactional at least in my brain

00:03:54.300 --> 00:04:00.760
and so for me I’ve sort of tried to tip
it to think like Okay well I’m just trying

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.890
to find other like-minded people who I connect
with.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:11.810
And then try to pursue that great feeling
of putting a movie on the screen or telling

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:17.980
a story or doing something and it’s not
just movies, it can be anything.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.790
Any sort of story that movies people.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:25.860
If we can find a way to connect on that, we
can become allies.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:31.270
We can fight for each other and be in the
trenches together and that’s a really beautiful

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:38.760
thing since I’ve taken that approach.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:46.500
Like I said I’m sort of super new at this
whole pursuing filmmaking career.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:55.680
But I do know that if you just don’t give
up and just keep meeting people, connecting

00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:02.870
with people who you like, and they like you
back, eventually something is going to happen.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:10.250
I don’t remember what the quote is but something
along the lines of the people who get lucky,

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:14.070
luck it opportunity meets preparation.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:17.230
That’s what luck is.

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:22.090
The more opportunities you have, the more
people that you get to start to know, that

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:26.630
know what you do and like what you do, eventually
there will be an opportunity for you to step

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.560
up and do something.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:32.990
There will be long stretches of time where
nothing happens and it feels like you’re

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:35.240
not making any progress.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:39.760
I literally just got out of a long stretch
of time where I felt that way.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.650
I was just like “What am I doing out here?

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.130
I want to move back home.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:44.450
I’m wasting my time.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:46.150
It’s super expensive to live out here.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.360
This is awful.”

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.970
But something twisted, something turned in
my brain.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:57.170
I was like “You know what, I may not know
anybody at these big studios that could get

00:05:57.170 --> 00:06:04.400
me a movie, but I do know a lot of people
out here that are on my level (sorry I shouldn’t

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:13.060
say level) but are on their same progression
in their journey.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:18.630
I know all of these people and what I can
do is just connect with the ones that I feel

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.550
get me and understand me.

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:25.080
And I started that process like 4 months ago.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:30.230
And it’s been amazing how many opportunities
have come from that.

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:33.540
Like “Okay, I know this writer who is in
my class.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:37.669
Let’s just grab coffee and talk to each
other and see how we might be able to help

00:06:37.669 --> 00:06:38.840
each other.”

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:41.780
And that’s been phenomenal.

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:45.730
You can get your script to people that way.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:55.720
I have a friend who ended up getting representation
because she ended up meeting with her friend

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:58.510
who were repped by…a rep.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:06.100
Anyone who was repped by someone they went
and met with them and basically felt it out.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.040
Is this a good fit first?

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:13.400
Do I feel like I connect with this person
and if they did and everything seemed right

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:20.100
she would be like “Hey, it might be a huge
ask but would you take a look at my script?”

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.380
And not asking “Hey, would you take a look
and give it to your rep?”

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:24.870
Just like “Hey, will you read it?

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:27.800
And if you like it, could you maybe pass it
on?

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.669
If not, no harm, no foul.”

00:07:29.669 --> 00:07:33.030
And they seemed to be pretty successful doing
it that way.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:38.270
There are so many different avenues but there
is no real one way.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:41.660
Hollywood seems to be the wild, wild, west.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:45.500
And I think (at least for me) that’s what
makes it intriguing.

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:51.080
Of like “Man, the next thing could come
from anywhere.”

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:56.750
There is way more opportunity around us than
we feel.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:59.800
It’s only just a matter of focus and attention.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:06.130
If you focus on the world being abundant instead
of scarce then suddenly the world becomes

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.360
abundant.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:12.130
And I know it sounds really weird but I’ve
noticed that when I’ve made those conscious

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.300
choices, things seem to happen.

